- **tests/blitz-tests:** holds Blitz's integration tests, one test-target file per behavior under `tests/`, and three shared modules that are no target — `tests/common/mod.rs`, the stand checks' tables and helpers, each stated once, `tests/session_common/mod.rs`, what the checks that hold a session share, and, since 2026-10-19-shared-fixtures, `tests/fixtures/mod.rs`, the fixture boot and hold, the fixture pages more than one check reads and the held network stand-in `HeldNet`, each stated once (§3 Crate-local test helpers) (tests/blitz-tests/lib.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:1-6; tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:1-7; tests/blitz-tests/tests/fixtures/mod.rs:17-130), and one file that is declared a target and never built, `tests/all.rs` — upstream's single-binary target `all`, held in the manifest at `test = false` (§2 Directory pattern; tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:56-59); coverage spans accessibility, layout, text, paint, hit testing, input events, scrolling, style invalidation, DOM mutation leaks, network-driven stylesheet loading, four checks that arrived with the 2026-10-10 upstream merge — autofocus read by the attribute's presence (`autofocus_attribute`, 5), the `math-auto` text transform (`text_transform`, 3), an anonymous block keeping its percentage-height containing block (`anonymous_block_percentage_height`, 1) and an inline box's offset size under three writing modes (one test of `inline_fragment_rects`), the package's blitz-dom dev-dependency gaining the `autofocus` and `text-transform-icu` features for them (tests/blitz-tests/tests/autofocus_attribute.rs:27-50; tests/blitz-tests/tests/text_transform.rs:18-47; tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_percentage_height.rs:6-39; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inline_fragment_rects.rs:125-150;
 tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:17) —, five that arrived with the 2026-10-13 upstream merge (`434e0661`), each its own target — a restyled owner's anonymous-block text following it (`anonymous_block_restyle`, 10), a button and a button-like input centring their content after `default.css`'s button-input rule became `inline-block` (`button_alignment`, 16), removing `checked` unchecking a checkbox and a radio (`checked_attribute`, 2), a pointer leaving the document, a sub-document host or the window, or a finger lifted or cancelled, clearing hover with leave events (`pointer_leave`, 7, through a hand-written `ShellProvider`), and `DocumentConfig.ua_stylesheets` used as given, the default config taking the default sheet and a later sheet overriding an earlier (`ua_stylesheet_order`, 3) — the package gaining the dev-dependency `cursor-icon` for them (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_restyle.rs:10-48; tests/blitz-tests/tests/button_alignment.rs:20-24; tests/blitz-tests/tests/checked_attribute.rs:53-61; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pointer_leave.rs:28-52; tests/blitz-tests/tests/ua_stylesheet_order.rs:20-43) —, Dioxus integration (including the clearing of a falsy Dioxus `disabled`, tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_disabled.rs:1, and of each of the 28 boolean attributes the check names — the bridge's own list until 2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship, its predicate since then upstream's 28-name `is_bool_attr` (`inert` added), and since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness `inert` the check's 28th name (`BOOLEAN_ATTRS: [&str; 28]`), the attribute half only, `stand_keyboard` and `inert_subtree` pinning a truthy `inert` honoured, a falsy one cleared by the bridge — on both attribute paths and in both layout modes — a `hidden: false` element displayed and a snapshot node, a truthy or unlisted attribute kept
 — tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_boolean_attrs.rs:1), the seven_guis headless stand — each lean task mounted in TaskShell offline at the pinned viewport with the bundled font, fresh-boot and incremental `dom_string` identity, one driven interaction per task, timer ticks, one stable element id per element in both layout modes, the same id across a re-render, a remount (fresh `NodeId`s bar the four document-skeleton elements) and a fresh process — the test binary re-executing its own `#[ignore]` child `ids_in_a_child_process` — and the id carried as AccessKit `author_id` on every element node and none other, the 15 controls' roles and names — and since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions every tree node of the four lean tasks in the nine interactive roles named, at least `controls(task).len()` of them per task, `crud-list` reading `People` in the tree and the snapshot by `common::REGION_NAMES`; the tree read through `&dyn blitz_dom::Document`, the call `AccessibilityState::update_tree` makes, equal to `harness.doc.accessibility_tree()` and carrying on every `author_id` its node's `element_id`, none empty, all digits or holding `0x`; and after a drained changed set a Tab and an Enter each leaving `has_changes()` true, that tree's focus and `counter-value`'s name following (`stand_accessibility_ids` 8, 5 until then, run by the `a11y` leg since then; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:255-308; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:310-352; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:363-410) —, the ids after a re-render and the Tab order of `common::tab_order` — CRUD's restated at 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness to six stops, `back-btn`, `crud-filter`, `crud-list`, `crud-name`, `crud-surname`, `crud-create` (five until then), the three other tasks' unchanged, and each lean task's snapshot in both layout modes
 — every node carrying id, role, name, state and bounds, its ids the accessibility tree's `author_id`s, its roles and names that tree's, the tree following the TaskShell, each control rendered at boot inside the viewport at its bounding client rect, state as the engine reads it, the snapshot deterministic and following a re-render, each control's state proven through real input in both layout modes — a disabled control reading not enabled until the app enables it (a `disabled="false"` and a bare `disabled` in parsed markup included), typed text reading back as the value, the range input reading the app's duration, exactly the focused control reading focused after a click, a Tab press and Shift+Tab, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states exactly the active flight mode reading pressed and the reading swapping with the mode, exactly the selected CRUD row reading selected across a move, a Delete and a filter edit, and a date that is no date reading invalid on both date inputs — no other node reading pressed, selected or invalid, and every node's three readings asserted equal to its accessibility node's by the file's `stated` helper (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:60-87; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:367-496) —, and, on an in-file fixture booted with the stand's options, a checkbox and a radio reading checked after a click, a typed password reading the fixed mask and appearing in no snapshot or accessibility-tree field, and a textarea named by `aria-label` reading empty before typing and its typed text back as its value, exactly it reading focused after the click (`a_textarea_reads_back_typed_text`, the eighth test the file gained, of eleven since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, read red with the `textarea` arm of the snapshot's `value` deleted — the one mutant the Epoch 4 code audit left alive
 — and green on the restored tree: tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:698-725, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-09-audit-corrections-agent-surfaces/evidence/controls.md) —, each lean task's screen as the snapshot's text (`Snapshot::to_text`) in both layout modes — one line per snapshot node carrying its role, name, id, state and bounds, nested by indent, every id on exactly one line, each screen under its in-file ceiling and under `SNAPSHOT_TEXT_BUDGET` (10,000 bytes; the largest, Crud, reads 2049 since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states — 2034 before it), CRUD after one Create longer and still inside it, the text the same across two calls, the two layout modes and a second boot, `focused` on no line at boot and on exactly `back-btn`'s after a Tab press, and, on two fixtures booted with the stand's options — the shared password page `fixtures::password_labelled` and an in-file file-input page —, a typed password and a file input's authored path reading the quoted mask and occurring nowhere in the text —, the diff of the snapshots taken before and after a step (`Snapshot::diff`) in both layout modes — a click on `counter-increment` naming `counter-value`, Create naming the new row added and Delete naming it removed, a click on a text input, a Tab press and Shift+Tab each naming exactly the controls whose `focused` reading moved, a typed character naming its text input, delivered ticks naming the elapsed time and the progress bar they widen, a pump with nothing pending on each lean task and a click on a disabled control reading an empty diff and a false `has_changes`, every step held against the file's own reading of the two snapshots and equal across the two layout modes, and, on three fixtures booted with the stand's options
 — two in-file and the shared password page `fixtures::password_labelled` —, an element hidden and shown by attribute leaving and returning with its descendants, a typed password named once and only by the fixed mask, and a rewritten label naming the input it labels —, the ids held across code edits — a before/after pair of same-named components per edit, in both layout modes: each lean task under an edited shell, keyed elements under every edit, anchored elements under an edit outside their anchor, a behaviour edit, and the edits inside an anchor measured on positional ids only — and every actionable element of the four lean tasks and of Home reading an author key (`DioxusDocument::unkeyed_actionable` empty) in both layout modes and across state, and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, of all seven tasks — `unkeyed_actionable()` 0 · 0 · 0 on Temperature Converter · Circle Drawer · Cells in both layout modes (2 · 3 · 676 until then), Circle Drawer's dialog open included, the three tasks keyed by added `id:` lines alone (`temp-celsius`, `temp-fahrenheit`, `circle-undo`, `circle-redo`, `circle-canvas`, `circle-diameter`, `circle-close`, `cell-{A..Z}{0..25}` on the 676 data cells, `cell-input`), no CSS selecting by them and no other markup line moved (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_actionable_keys.rs:142-144; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_actionable_keys.rs:153-155) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_id_edits.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_actionable_keys.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_boot.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_counter.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_flight_booker.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_timer.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_crud.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_element_ids.rs:1;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_id_persistence.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_text.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_diff.rs:1) — accessible names from `aria-label` and `<label>` association, and a plain document's tree carrying no `author_id` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_names.rs:1) — and, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, the accessibility builder's three state attributes read by value on a parsed page, in both layout modes — `accessibility_states` 5: `aria-selected` reads `true` and `false` and nothing else (9 rows), `aria-pressed` its three values and nothing else (10), `aria-invalid` its values and an unrecognized one as true (11), each on a role that supports the attribute and one that does not, the row counts asserted; `aria-checked`'s `true` · `false` · `mixed` written as the toggle on the five checkable roles alone, and a native checkbox or radio reading neither `aria-checked` nor `aria-pressed` (`aria_checked_reads_its_three_values_on_a_checkable_role_alone`); and `aria-pressed` on a checkable role reading nothing, a 5,500-character `aria-checked` nowhere in the tree (`aria_pressed_on_a_checkable_role_reads_nothing_and_a_long_aria_checked_is_nowhere`) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_states.rs:134-316), run by the workspace `test` leg, per package, the `stand-repeat` leg (a named `--test` of its list) and the `a11y` leg, one of its fourteen files; blitz-dom holds no unit test of the builder's reads, and no check reads the three states as the platform adapter hands them to an assistive technology — no stand binary builds an adapter and the dev host's AT-SPI bus reads inactive, the stand's normal dependency graph holding neither `accesskit_xplat` nor `accesskit_winit` (`cargo tree --locked -p seven_guis -e normal` probe 0, as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-24-a11y-re-read/report.md), so no check in the `a11y` leg reaches the adapter crossing
 — a gap owned since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions by a `.andromeda/residuals.md` line that reads `re-carried:0.2.0`, at an active assistive technology this version does not reach, on the founder's F1 «Пока нет, перенести (Рекомендую)», the tree the shell hands the adapter and the refresh's two halves proven headlessly on the stand at that chunk (`stand_accessibility_ids` above) (as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-snapshot-states/report.md) — and, since 2026-10-17-upstream-sync-engine-debts's upstream merge (upstream #859 · #1013, at `23b9b26a9`), two checks of the builder's merged name and description reads on a parsed page, asserted through test-that's `verify_that!`: `accessibility_label` 13 (a `<label for>` and a wrapping `<label>` each naming a `select` and a `textarea`, and a `<label>` naming no hidden `input`, HTML's labelable elements (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_label.rs:309-432); `aria-label` as the label; `aria-labelledby` as `labelled_by` for one and for two nodes; an id the DOM does not hold ignored; the targets' text as the label; `aria-labelledby` outranking `aria-label` and content; a self-reference with nested text; a target's own `aria-label`; hidden targets naming without being referenced; the fall back to `aria-label` when the targets hold no text — tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_label.rs:8-447) and `accessibility_description` 3 (`aria-description` as the description; `aria-describedby` targets as `described_by` in order; targets outside the tree excluded — tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_description.rs:8-101), each its own auto-discovered target, run by the workspace `test` leg, per package and the `a11y` leg;
 upstream's `focus_within` 7 (`:focus-within` matching the focused element's ancestors and clearing on blur, a `display: contents` ancestor, focus set before the first layout pass, the focused subtree removed, moved, and moved out of the document, and a node outside the document not focused — tests/blitz-tests/tests/focus_within.rs:35-192) and `focus_redraw` 4 (a focus set, a blur and a Tab each requesting one redraw and a refocus of the same node none, counted on a `RecordingShell` `ShellProvider` — tests/blitz-tests/tests/focus_redraw.rs:73-120), taken at 2026-10-19-upstream-sync-visual-lint-and-real-app-readiness, each its own auto-discovered target, run by the workspace `test` leg and `run all` and not by the `a11y` leg — not among its fourteen — or `run stand`;
 upstream's `hit_test_dropped_nodes` 1 (a hit on a parsed page skips a node dropped since the last resolve, so it answers no removed node — tests/blitz-tests/tests/hit_test_dropped_nodes.rs:32-82), read red with its engine hunks to `node/node.rs` and `layout/paint_tree.rs` reversed and green with them, its own auto-discovered target, run by the workspace `test` leg and `run all` and not by the `a11y` leg — not among its fourteen — or `run stand`; `accessibility_merged_states` 3 — `aria-expanded` reads `true` and `false` and nothing else, `aria-disabled` sets disabled for `true` alone, `aria-level` reads its number less one and the heading defaults (`default_level_for_tag` / `default_level_for_role`), each table's row count asserted, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_merged_states.rs:88-157); `accessibility_active_descendant_unread` 1 — a focused listbox carrying `aria-activedescendant` reads focus and no active descendant, in both layout modes, the unread attribute pinned (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_active_descendant_unread.rs:39-81); `inert_subtree` 4 — Tab and Shift+Tab skip an inert subtree, a hit passes through it, the tree holds no node for it, and removing `inert` restores focus, hit and tree, the focus-fixup limit (a node made inert keeps focus) pinned there, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/inert_subtree.rs:68-194); each its own auto-discovered target, run by the workspace `test` leg and per package — `accessibility_active_descendant_unread` and `inert_subtree` also by the `stand-repeat` leg (named `--test`s of its list), `accessibility_merged_states` not — and by the `a11y` leg;
 the snapshot's `enabled` reads the `disabled` attribute, not AccessKit, so `aria-disabled` moves no snapshot reading — and process telemetry — stdout stays silent, the scrub redacts, the panic hook logs one event and chains, init is idempotent, and a record from a target outside the sink's allowlist writes nothing at any level under a `RUST_LOG` directive naming it, native and bridged alike, while an escher record prints and an engine record prints redacted (`telemetry_drop`, the test binary re-run on its one `#[ignore]` child) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_stdout_silent.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_scrub.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_panic_hook.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_init_idempotent.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_drop.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/incremental_oracle.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/whitespace_modes.rs:15; tests/blitz-tests/tests/paint_order.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pointer_events.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/style_property_invalidation.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inner_html_leak.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/link_rel_attribute.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:1); and the driver session over the stand, in both layout modes where a screen is read
 — on one `escher_driver::Session` a later command reads what an earlier one left (counter clicks, a created CRUD row, focus after a Tab press, timer time moved only by delivered ticks: `stand_session_state`, 3), a control's stable id before a command is its accessibility node's `author_id` after it and a CRUD row keeps its person's id across a later Create and under a filter (`stand_session_ids`, 2), a held instance reads as a fresh boot and its mount and viewport hold after commands (`stand_session_fresh`, 2), start · attach · stop and each edge over the Unix-domain socket with the `0700` directory and `0600` socket asserted (`stand_session_lifecycle`, 2 and its two `#[ignore]` host children, `session_host` and `session_host_with_a_short_expiry`: since 2026-10-10-driver-cli its first test also runs a call and reads a refused one over the socket and sends five raw lines outside the grammar and one wrong-version line through the live socket, each refused with nothing run, and its second proves a host with no request for its expiry ends as `stop` does, the state directory watched and `attach` never polled), and nothing of the screen is written by a session host that installs no log sink (`stand_session_quiet`, 1 and its `#[ignore]` host child `session_host_with_typed_text`; its limit is in §5), and since 2026-10-19-session-recording a recorded session — `stand_session_recording` 3, declaring `mod session_common;`: a recorded session keeps each answer whole but a shot's image — every record ending with its kept line, no `png` and no shot's first 64 base64 characters — and replays through `Check::replay` on each lean task in both layout modes, each script ending `snapshot` · `screenshot`, so the shot path's kept form is covered on each unix OS CI runs (linux, macOS; the file is unix only, as recording is);
 a password typed in a recorded session is kept as the stand-in, 0 sentinel occurrences and a secret of another length leaving byte-identical files; a recording directory open to its group is refused with nothing written (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_recording.rs:108-286), and since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay the committed checks replayed — `stand_replay` 3, declaring `mod session_common;`, not unix-gated: the two committed Counter checks hold in both layout modes, turn red at step 1 (the command line's) and step 3 (the MCP role's) on a test-local `Counter` variant of the task's own name with every earlier step held and `changed` among the keys, a check on another app runs nothing, and neither check holds a `png` key or a shot's first 64 base64 characters (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_replay.rs:81-110; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_replay.rs:198-234; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_replay.rs:236-258) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_state.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_ids.rs:1-5; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_fresh.rs:1-5; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_lifecycle.rs:1-7; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_quiet.rs:1-7) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-session/report.md; and settle on a held instance (`stand_settle`, 8, each in both layout modes and calling no sleep, no clock and no pump or tick of its own): a Timer step run through `Session::act` returns reading `Elapsed: 0.3s`, having read `0.0s` inside the step after the delivery; a settle on an idle lean task is `Settled { passes: 1, animating: false }` and changes nothing — the same snapshot text, a false change flag after a drain, no focus, a first Tab on `back-btn`;
 and on in-file fixtures a write made in a `mounted` handler is present after the step, a load in flight reads `NotSettled(Loads)` until the check answers it, its `@import` included, a running animation reads `animating: true` and does not hold the step, a hover that moves with layout is resolved before the step returns, an instance that renders on every pass ends at the bound as `Render` and a hover that never rests as `Layout` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_settle.rs:1-9) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-settle-detection/report.md; the driver's calls run through `Session::run` on a held stand session, in both layout modes — `stand_act_ids` 2 (for each of the 77 nodes of the four lean tasks' snapshots, the 15 controls among them, the id the snapshot lists is the `author_id` of the one accessibility node carrying it, the element `element_ids()` resolves it to is that node's, and a driver `click` naming it is accepted on 70 and refused on the 7 the check states from the measured stand, each with its cause — the three disabled controls as `disabled`, and each task's `task-header-spacer`, a box with no height at whose centre the header is hit, as `covered` — both row counts asserted, while an id no element carries is refused `not-found`; for each of the 12 controls a click is accepted on, the driver's diff equals a twin's selector click, settled — not empty for every one since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, a click focusing a button as it does a text input and the slider: 15 control rows over `controls(task)` change the screen at boot (18 rows, `back-btn` ×4; 9 until then, the Timer's slider `timer-duration` the ninth since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction) — and for the 3 it is refused on, the twin's selector click changes nothing;
 the Timer's Reset resets nothing at boot beyond taking focus, so what it resets is read after an `advance`), `stand_act_diff` 6 (each step's returned diff equals the check's own `before.diff(&after)` and names exactly the nodes stated for it on the four lean tasks — a click, a choice, an advance, a typed name, Create adding `crud-person-3` and Delete removing it; a click on the heading returns settled with an empty diff; the two modes return equal diffs; on a fixture a password typed by the driver occurs 0 times in what the call returns and its entry reads `MASKED_VALUE`), `stand_act_timer` 4 (Reset then `advance` 300 returns settled with `advanced_ms` 300 and `Elapsed: 0.3s` in the returned diff, every `advance` reporting exactly the `ms` asked and the harness clock moving by exactly that; an `advance` on a Counter, FlightBooker or Crud session, none carrying a time step, moves the clock and settles; on an animated fixture an `advance` reports exactly what was asked whatever the step does — the step handed exactly `ms`, `advanced_ms` = `ms`, the clock moved by exactly `ms`, nothing added or removed, `fx-press` changed exactly when the step pressed it (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18); a click beside a running animation returns settled), `stand_act_refused` 3 (a table of four refused calls — an unknown verb, a missing argument, an id of 1024 bytes that names nothing, the id of a row the driver just deleted — each returns its cause, the id no screen of the session read as `not-found` and the deleted row's, which an earlier screen read, as `stale`, leaves the snapshot equal and reads as a text holding none of the supplied bytes; an id of 1025 bytes is `malformed` before any lookup;
